<h2>4. The Four Big Systems</h2>
<h3>Tasks, Logs &amp; Events</h3>
<p>Everything that happens gets logged. Every task, every communication, every event. If it happened, it\'s in the system.</p>
<p><em>When Eileen called to ask about her application timeline, that call was logged. When the assessor visited, that visit was logged. When the crew finished the roof, that completion was logged.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href="tasks-logs-events.md">Tasks, Logs &amp; Events</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Document Bucket</h3>
<p>All files are organized by case in a standardized folder structure. Every document has a consistent naming convention.</p>
<p><em>The Bailey\'s intake form, assessment photos, contract, and completion certificate are all stored in their case folder, organized and easy to find.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href="document-storage.md">Document Storage &amp; Generation</a></p>
</blockquote>
<h3>Progress Tracker</h3>
<p>An immutable ledger of what happened, when, and by whom. Nothing is ever deleted or overwritten.</p>
<p><em>Every step of the Bailey\'s journey—from application to completion—is recorded forever.</em></p>
<h3>Quick Add</h3>
<p>One-click logging from the field. Click "+ Add Event," select the task type, enter date and notes, and save.</p>
<p><em>The crew lead marked "Roof Repair Complete" from their phone before they even left the Bailey property.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href="quick-add-progress-tasks.md">Quick Add Progress Tasks</a></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>5. Quick Add Explained</h2>
<p>Quick Add is designed for busy people in the field. You don\'t need to fill out a long form—just the essentials.</p>
<p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Click <strong>"+ Add Event"</strong> from any case</li>
<li>Select the <strong>task type</strong> (ASSESS, SCOPE, START, COMPLETE, PROGRESS)</li>
<li>Enter the <strong>date</strong> and any <strong>notes</strong></li>
<li>Upload <strong>photos or documents</strong> (optional)</li>
<li>Click <strong>Save</strong></li>
</ol>
<p><em>The assessor visited the Bailey home, took photos, and logged the assessment in under two minutes using Quick Add.</em></p>
<p><strong>What happens after you save:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The entry goes to the <strong>Unverified</strong> queue</li>
<li>A <strong>Task Rabbit</strong> reviews and approves it</li>
<li>Once approved, it counts toward metrics</li>
<li>All changes are permanent in the ledger</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>6. What Happens After I Submit Something</h2>
